WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:08.266
Tim and his mom walked up to Aunt Rosa's house.

2
00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:16.446
"I know this isn't ideal," Mom said, "but Aunt Rosa and I have to work Saturday shifts now.

3
00:00:16.447 --> 00:00:19.529
I don't want to leave you home alone."

4
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.919
"But why do I have to stay here with Andre?" Tim asked.

5
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.741
"He's so much older than me, and we barely even talk when we see each other.

6
00:00:28.742 --> 00:00:32.418
All he does is stay in his room."

7
00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:37.809
"You and your cousin might have more in common than you think," Mom said.

8
00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:41.788
"I doubt it," Tim mumbled.

9
00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:45.954
Inside the house Andre was nowhere to be seen.

10
00:00:45.955 --> 00:00:52.430
Tim plopped down on the sofa and turned on the TV.

11
00:00:52.431 --> 00:00:55.794
"Boring as usual," Tim thought.

12
00:00:55.795 --> 00:01:02.548
"Yo," a voice said suddenly. "You play the piano, don't you?"

13
00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:06.991
It was Andre. Tim looked at him, confused.

14
00:01:06.992 --> 00:01:11.919
"Yeah," Tim said. "Why?"

15
00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.966
"Follow me."

16
00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:19.592
Andre led Tim toward his room.

17
00:01:19.593 --> 00:01:24.576
Tim realized that he had never seen the inside of Andre's room before.

18
00:01:24.577 --> 00:01:31.547
Several Keep Out! stickers were crookedly plastered on the door.

19
00:01:31.548 --> 00:01:37.211
"Welcome to my music studio," Andre said as they entered.

20
00:01:37.212 --> 00:01:46.243
Tim blinked. It looked like a normal bedroom, not the studios he'd seen in music videos and on TV.

21
00:01:46.244 --> 00:01:54.279
The only musical things he saw were a piano keyboard and a mic connected to Andre's computer via USB cables.

22
00:01:54.280 --> 00:02:00.457
"It probably doesn't look like much," Andre said, noticing Tim's reaction.

23
00:02:00.458 --> 00:02:05.081
"Many amateur musicians like me set up small home studios.

24
00:02:05.082 --> 00:02:11.095
Recording equipment and software aren't as expensive as most people would think."

25
00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:17.712
"So you record yourself playing the piano and singing on your computer?" Tim asked.

26
00:02:17.713 --> 00:02:22.645
"Sometimes," Andre said, "but I can do more than that.

27
00:02:22.646 --> 00:02:33.136
With my music program and this keyboard, I can pretty much play any sound I want—real instruments, electronic sounds, and even dog barks!"

28
00:02:33.137 --> 00:02:37.613
Tim laughed.

29
00:02:37.614 --> 00:02:41.530
"Here, let me show you a song I've been working on."

30
00:02:41.531 --> 00:02:46.052
Andre opened a file on his music program.

31
00:02:46.053 --> 00:02:48.524
"First I came up with this melody.

32
00:02:48.525 --> 00:02:55.361
I played it on the keyboard and chose the sound I wanted to use."

33
00:02:55.362 --> 00:03:02.097
Tim listened to Andre's electronic melody. "Is that the whole song?"

34
00:03:02.098 --> 00:03:06.414
"No, that's just one track," Andre said.

35
00:03:06.415 --> 00:03:10.009
He pointed to some jagged lines on the computer screen.

36
00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:13.543
"Each instrument I use is on a separate track.

37
00:03:13.544 --> 00:03:19.083
After I made the first track, I added drums and bass."

38
00:03:19.084 --> 00:03:29.575
He played the individual tracks for Tim.

39
00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:33.627
"I can mix the tracks together to make the song."

40
00:03:33.628 --> 00:03:42.792
He pressed Play, and Tim heard all three tracks playing simultaneously.

41
00:03:42.793 --> 00:03:47.694
Tim was surprised by how passionate Andre was about his music.

42
00:03:47.695 --> 00:03:50.820
He'd never seen this side of his cousin before.

43
00:03:50.821 --> 00:03:54.770
"That's so cool!" he exclaimed.

44
00:03:54.771 --> 00:04:00.068
"Thanks," Andre said with a sigh.

45
00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:05.039
"But I'm not finished yet. That was just the verse portion of the song.

46
00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:10.858
I can't think of a catchy melody for the chorus—the part that repeats between verses.

47
00:04:10.859 --> 00:04:13.936
That's the part listeners will remember most.

48
00:04:13.937 --> 00:04:16.856
Do you think you can come up with something?"

49
00:04:16.857 --> 00:04:20.213
"Me?" Tim asked nervously.

50
00:04:20.214 --> 00:04:27.047
He'd been playing the piano for seven years, but he'd never composed his own melodies before.

51
00:04:27.048 --> 00:04:29.776
"I guess I can try."

52
00:04:29.777 --> 00:04:34.887
He took a seat at the keyboard and listened to Andre's melody a few more times.

53
00:04:34.888 --> 00:04:39.030
He tried to imagine some possible melodies in his head.

54
00:04:39.031 --> 00:04:52.127
Then he put his fingers on the keys and started to play.

55
00:04:52.128 --> 00:04:55.252
"How about something like this?"

56
00:04:55.253 --> 00:04:59.731
"Perfect!" Andre looked impressed.

57
00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:13.285
He played the chorus with Tim's melody mixed with the rest of the instruments.

58
00:05:13.286 --> 00:05:22.947
"Now I just need to arrange the parts into an introduction, verses, chorus, and an ending—sort of like the structure of an essay.

59
00:05:22.948 --> 00:05:46.189
I think I'll start it like this."

60
00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:51.766
"What will you do when you're finished composing the song?" Tim asked.

61
00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:54.823
"I'm going to rap over it and make a demo song.

62
00:05:54.824 --> 00:05:59.762
Then I'll upload it to the internet and send the link to major record labels.

63
00:05:59.763 --> 00:06:01.454
Maybe they'll give me advice.

64
00:06:01.455 --> 00:06:06.421
Or who knows, if I'm lucky, maybe one of them will offer me a contract."

65
00:06:06.422 --> 00:06:10.649
"You know," Tim said, "I can sing too.

66
00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:15.625
What if you rap the verses and I sing the chorus?"

67
00:06:15.626 --> 00:06:22.886
Andre's face lit up. "Great idea! Start writing your own lyrics for the chorus.

68
00:06:22.887 --> 00:06:26.200
I'll finish the song arrangement and write my lyrics too.

69
00:06:26.201 --> 00:06:30.383
Then we can record our vocals."

70
00:06:30.384 --> 00:06:32.951
Tim grabbed a pencil and some paper.

71
00:06:32.952 --> 00:06:41.921
"I guess spending Saturdays with Andre will be pretty fun after all," he thought.

